    <string name="settings_privacy_note">No tracking, no telemetry, no Google services. The app only talks to planetfoss.net and to the sites you open – and, only if you switch it on, fetches the tracker filter list (easylist.to). If you switch on Settings → Anonymous counting, opened articles are counted for the sources as a daily total – no identifier. Which lists the app loads, planetfoss.net counts as daily totals, like page views on the website.</string>
    <string name="settings_privacy_note_ads">No tracking, no telemetry, no Google services. The app only talks to planetfoss.net and to the sites you open – and, only if you switch it on, fetches the tracker filter list (easylist.to). If you switch on Settings → Anonymous counting, opened articles are counted for the sources as a daily total – no identifier. Which lists the app loads, planetfoss.net counts as daily totals, like page views on the website. Sponsor cards you see are always counted for the sponsors, as on the website: which card, where and in which language – no identifier.</string>
